<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Delft</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Delft is a city in the province of South Holland, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a>, between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rotterdam">Rotterdam</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/the-hague">The Hague</a>, which received town rights in 1246. It prospered from brewing, cloth and later the blue-and-white Delftware pottery. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-the-silent">William the Silent</a> was assassinated in the Prinsenhof there in 1584 and lies in its New Church, the burial place of the House of Orange, and the painter <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/johannes-vermeer">Johannes Vermeer</a> worked in the city.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/delft.jpg" alt="Delft" width="320" height="220" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Zairon · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Delft_Blick_von_der_Nieuwe_Kerk_auf_die_Oude_Kerk_1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
